import{_ as t,o as a,c as i,a2 as r}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const f=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 120 | Realm Refinement · Transform Origin Realm | Predatory Faction vs. Symbiotic Faction","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 120 | Realm Refinement · Transform Origin Realm | Predatory Faction vs. Symbiotic Faction","no":120,"module":1,"tags":["Realm","Transform Origin Realm","Predatory Faction","Symbiotic Faction","System Comparison"],"related":["04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise","01-Anchor Symbiotic Civilization Manifesto","14-Unified Cultivation Realm Classification"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0120_模块1-化元境-掠夺派vs共生派对比.md","filePath":"en/0120_模块1-化元境-掠夺派vs共生派对比.md"}'),o={name:"en/0120_模块1-化元境-掠夺派vs共生派对比.md"};function n(s,e,l,c,h,d){return a(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[r('<h1 id="entry-120-transform-origin-realm-predatory-faction-vs-symbiotic-faction-detailed-comparison" tabindex="-1">Entry 120 | Transform Origin Realm: Predatory Faction vs. Symbiotic Faction Detailed Comparison <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-120-transform-origin-realm-predatory-faction-vs-symbiotic-faction-detailed-comparison" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 120 | Transform Origin Realm: Predatory Faction vs. Symbiotic Faction Detailed Comparison&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 1 · In-Depth Realm Refinement | Baseline references: Documents 04, 01, 14</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-what-you-transform-is-a-creation-or-a-weapon" tabindex="-1">Introduction: What you transform is a creation or a weapon <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-what-you-transform-is-a-creation-or-a-weapon" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: What you transform is a creation or a weapon&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Condensed Realm (Entry 113) competed over &quot;how you bank your nest egg&quot;; the Transform Realm competes over &quot;what you actually transform.&quot; The Predatory faction transforms energy into weapons, enslavement tools, and others&#39; &quot;refining material&quot;; the Symbiotic faction transforms energy into healing, infrastructure, and craft shared by all Myriad Races. The same transformation spell, different paths, and the civilizational meaning of the product is worlds apart.</p><p>The six top-level axioms are the watershed of the two paths: the anti-predation axiom — energy source and product use together define the path; the republican axiom of Myriad Races — the Symbiotic sees Myriad Races as fellow cultivators, the Predatory sees all beings as material; the collective ascension axiom — the Symbiotic transforms for ascension, the Predatory transforms for predation, eliminating talent underuse; the causal self-discipline axiom — all Symbiotic products are reportable and traceable; the law-first axiom — the Transform Realm comparison framework is stable and self-consistent, never rewritten for plot convenience, and infinitely expandable without collapse; the universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-systematic-comparison-table" tabindex="-1">I. Systematic Comparison Table <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-systematic-comparison-table" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Systematic Comparison Table&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Predatory · Transform Realm</th><th>Symbiotic · Transform Realm</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Energy source</td><td>High-grade energy refined from predation</td><td>Legitimate circulation energy, Myriad Race origin two-way circulation</td></tr><tr><td>Transformation direction</td><td>Weapons, enslavement tools, refining others</td><td>Healing, infrastructure, craft shared by all Myriad Races</td></tr><tr><td>Products</td><td>Weapons and material, lost when the master falls</td><td>Creations and craft, written into the 300 systems, passed down</td></tr><tr><td>Breakthrough cost</td><td>Refined impurities congeal, hazards amplify</td><td>Real cost + anchor monitoring, reversible</td></tr><tr><td>Destination</td><td>Efficiency ceiling: entangled with impurities and blood debts</td><td>Mature craft, direct to the Law Realm &quot;first bottleneck&quot;</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="ii-the-three-fallacies-projected-in-the-transform-realm" tabindex="-1">II. The Three Fallacies Projected in the Transform Realm <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-the-three-fallacies-projected-in-the-transform-realm" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. The Three Fallacies Projected in the Transform Realm&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Document 04&#39;s three fallacies are especially clear in this realm:</p><ol><li>Cosmological fallacy: treating evolution as zero-sum, transformation means &quot;steal and refine&quot;</li><li>Ethical fallacy: treating all beings as refining material</li><li>Efficiency fallacy: believing refining predatory energy is fastest — impurities and will traces make late-stage transformation costs runaway</li></ol><h2 id="iii-enlightened-predators-even-benevolence-cannot-save-weapon-craft" tabindex="-1">III. Enlightened Predators: Even Benevolence Cannot Save Weapon Craft <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-enlightened-predators-even-benevolence-cannot-save-weapon-craft" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Enlightened Predators: Even Benevolence Cannot Save Weapon Craft&quot;">​</a></h2><p>&quot;Enlightened predators,&quot; even if relatively benevolent, still serve their transformation craft the patronage logic of &quot;the strong protect all beings&quot; — craft is monopolized, weapons are dispensed, beings depend. He stands atop the predatory system, and the predatory system&#39;s ceiling is his ceiling.</p><h2 id="iv-why-the-predatory-faction-must-historically-regress" tabindex="-1">IV. Why the Predatory Faction Must Historically Regress <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-why-the-predatory-faction-must-historically-regress" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Why the Predatory Faction Must Historically Regress&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Predatory transformation craft hinges on the top individual: while the strong lives, craft is monopolized by him; when he falls, craft is buried with him. The symbiotic faction writes craft into the anchor network and the 300 systems, learnable by all, passed down through generations — this is precisely the structural answer to eliminating historical regression.</p><h2 id="v-the-righteous-rogue-the-open-contract-of-transformation-craft" tabindex="-1">V. The Righteous Rogue: The Open Contract of Transformation Craft <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-the-righteous-rogue-the-open-contract-of-transformation-craft" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. The Righteous Rogue: The Open Contract of Transformation Craft&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Lin Hao&#39;s deduction of Path D · Humanoid Artificial Dao-Rule Soul Rings is essentially tearing up old law at the transformation layer: replacing the predatory production of hunting-and-stripping rings with the industrial production of artificial Dao rules. One who chooses craft openness in the Transform Realm is already closer to hyper-multiverse civilization than the enlightened predator trapped atop the predatory system.</p><h2 id="vi-cross-realm-handover-weapon-craft-vs-creation-craft-divide-in-the-law-realm" tabindex="-1">VI. Cross-Realm Handover: Weapon Craft vs. Creation Craft Divide in the Law Realm <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-cross-realm-handover-weapon-craft-vs-creation-craft-divide-in-the-law-realm" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Cross-Realm Handover: Weapon Craft vs. Creation Craft Divide in the Law Realm&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The predatory weapon craft refined in the Transform Realm and the symbiotic creation craft practiced draw their first true efficiency gap at Law Realm breakthrough. Weapon-craft cultivators entering the law understanding stage will find the high-grade energy they refined carries the original owner&#39;s will traces; these traces constantly interfere as they try to understand laws, making their law models forever impure. Creation-craft cultivators, with clean energy and mature craft as a base, find law understanding naturally smooth. The deeper divide: weapon craft is privately hoarded and cannot be written into the 300 systems; even if their cultivators reach the Law Realm, they must grope alone, and the knowledge ecology inevitably atrophies; creation craft is openly shared, and cultivators stand on the shoulders of Myriad Races&#39; craft accumulation to understand laws — this is the real cost of knowledge monopoly at cross-realm ascension.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Universal infinite backstop</strong>: the universal equal infinite law establishes that every being inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing have a guarantee, strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose, predation naturally loses meaning</li><li>Anti-energy waste: the Predatory faction wastes craft talent on weapons; the Symbiotic faction deploys talent toward creation</li><li>Anti-predation: cutting off &quot;refining predatory energy&quot; from the third realm, the path divide is real and effective</li><li>Tang-Luo upper limit comparison: Tang-Luo-style &quot;universal welfare&quot; is still patronage, craft depends on the strong; symbiotic craft is learnable by all</li><li>Myriad Races full coverage: the Predatory sees all beings as material, the Symbiotic sees Myriad Races as fellow cultivators; 99% coverage has no exceptions</li><li>Hyper-multiverse full openness: the Predatory monopolizes craft; the Symbiotic opens all tiers from the Transform Realm onward</li></ul><p>This divide also reveals a truth often overlooked: the Predatory faction&#39;s &quot;fast-track&quot; is actually a long-term liability. The energy and craft they refine at every realm carry original owner&#39;s will traces; these traces are inconspicuous at lower realms, but collect debts at cross-realm handover. The Symbiotic faction&#39;s slowness seems to lose out, but actually banks every realm as clean principal. Over time, the Predatory &quot;strong&quot; become burdened by traces, while the Symbiotic &quot;slow&quot; travel light toward origin.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The two paths in the Transform Realm compete not over who transforms faster, but what the transformed thing leaves to the world. The Predatory faction pours every effort to make weapons, only to find the weapons decay with them; the Symbiotic faction steadily writes craft into the system, and the works live on in Myriad Races&#39; hands through generations. The way you create has already written civilization&#39;s destination.</p><p>The Predatory long-term liability and Symbiotic long-term principal finally settle at cross-realm handover. This settlement process is quiet, but most just — it makes every realm&#39;s laziness nowhere to hide, and every realm&#39;s diligence earns compound interest.</p><p>In the final analysis, the Transform Realm Predatory vs. Symbiotic comparison described in this document is no isolated case — it operates within Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s overall coordinates; its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise</a> · <a href="./01-锚点共生文明宣言.html">01-Anchor Symbiotic Civilization Manifesto</a> · <a href="./14-修炼境界统一划分.html">14-Unified Cultivation Realm Classification</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',27)])])}const u=t(o,[["render",n]]);export{f as __pageData,u as default};
